  "body": "## What changed\nPart 1 of #261's triage: a path that generated with verify warnings now shows them in the viewport.\n- **Viewport:** every move a warning names (Gouge, ShankHit, SweepHit, RapidInStock, FixtureHit, NonFinite, Envelope, Scallop, both moves of a Crossing) draws in the palette's colour-vision-aware gouge colour instead of its feed / rapid / plunge colour. The first move of each folded warning line also gets a small 3-axis cross in that colour - the plunge red is close to the gouge red, so colour alone wouldn't single out a warned plunge. One cross per folded line, so a long shank run doesn't litter the view.\n- **Op page:** each folded warning line in the expanded status banner is a link (\"show this move in the viewport\"); a click centres the camera on that move's midpoint via the existing `actions::frame_at`, keeping zoom and orientation. View state only, not a command.\n- `RestUnjudged` marks and frames nothing (its index is a convention, not a place). A warning index past the end of the path is ignored, never indexed.\n- A path with no warnings draws exactly as before; no pixel snapshot changed.\n\nThe warned-move set is a pure app function (`crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs`); the drawing moved out of `interact.rs` into `crates/ui/src/path_lines.rs`. `shell.rs`, `egui_app/mod.rs` and `state.rs` are untouched.\n\nPart 2 (showing a path for a *refused* generation) is not included - it's a design call, so this PR says `Refs #261`.\n\n## Readings\n- Planted gouge ring: the warned set is exactly the plunge plus the 4 sides (not the retract rapid), and the first line frames (3.5, 3.5, 2).\n- Quick gate (app + ui suites): green except the known ones - `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag` (red on main, #344 / PR #345) and the GPU headless tests (no graphics adapter here).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- app: `warned_moves::tests::{every_located_kind_names_its_move_and_the_unjudged_note_names_none, the_mask_marks_named_moves_and_drops_out_of_range_ones, the_focus_is_the_move_midpoint_and_refuses_past_the_end}`; test binary `warned_moves`: `a_gouged_ring_marks_exactly_its_gouging_moves`, `a_clean_ring_marks_nothing`\n- ui: `path_lines::tests::{a_clean_path_draws_exactly_as_before, warned_moves_wear_the_gouge_colour_and_the_first_gets_a_cross, each_folded_line_frames_its_first_moves_midpoint, the_mark_follows_the_colour_vision_palette_and_the_dim}`, `operations::warning_fold_tests::each_folded_line_carries_its_groups_first_move`, `egui_app::layout::banner_tests::a_located_warning_line_reports_its_click_and_a_plain_line_does_not`\n\n## GUI check (why this stays a draft)\n1. Generate an op that warns (e.g. a contour with a short-flute tool deep enough for a holder hit, or a low clearance so a rapid passes through stock).\n2. The warned moves are gouge red (dark red under Deutan/Protan), with a small cross on each warning group's first move; other moves keep their colours.\n3. On its page, expand the status line; warning lines are underlined. Hover: \"show this move in the viewport\". Click: the camera centres on the move, zoom/orientation unchanged.\n4. A plain entry-note line isn't clickable; an op with no warnings looks as before.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/261-warned-moves.md`.\n\nChangelog: Warned toolpath moves are drawn in the gouge colour with a marker, and each warning line on the operation page centres the viewport on its move\n\nRefs #261\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
